 "notes": "A row is one inscription number with its five-position classification and the drawing line printed beside it. Coordinates are PDF points from the top-left corner of the page (595 by 841). row_centers_pdf holds the vertical midpoint of each number and classification block, top to bottom; the drawing line of a row lies about 2 pt above that midpoint (1.7 to 2.6 pt for 80 percent of the rows). x_extent_pdf runs from the leftmost to the rightmost printed ink of a column, covering the number field, the drawings, uncertainty underlines and continuation lines, and leaving out specks in the page margins and the handwritten annotation on page 139. Ten lines without a number block (pages 37, 48, 84 and 123) continue the numbered row above them; a physical side or line boundary does not make a new row, so they are listed under continuation_lines and left out of row_count. Counting them as rows would give 1857 lines. Full columns hold 36 line slots at a pitch of 19.7 to 19.9 pt; the five columns that carry two continuation lines hold 34 rows. The two readers agree on the row count of every column; the adjudicator's independent detection of the number blocks gives the same count in all 52 columns."
